{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/pulls/7612","id":4954437467,"node_id":"PR_kwDOS4Me3c8AAAABJ063Ww","html_url":"https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate/pull/7612","diff_url":"https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate/pull/7612.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate/pull/7612.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/issues/7612","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/pulls/7612/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/pulls/7612/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/issues/7612/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunchenguid/firstmate/statuses/4c60946a388715d1cfb0a65865f4c2193b0ca0c1","number":7612,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(bin): detect and alert on pending Claude permission prompts","user":{"login":"johntran-mudflap","id":167032618,"node_id":"U_kgDOCfS3Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/167032618?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johntran-mudflap","html_url":"https://github.com/johntran-mudflap","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johntran-mudflap/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johntran-mudflap/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johntran-mudflap/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johntran-mudflap/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johntran-mudflap/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johntran-mudflap/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johntran-mudflap/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johntran-mudflap/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johntran-mudflap/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What Changed\n- `bin/fm-composer-lib.sh` adds `fm_composer_permission_prompt`. It recognizes a Claude tool-permission dialog: a \"Do you want to …?\" row, then `1. Yes` and `<n>. No` options, with `Esc to cancel` as the last non-blank row. It extracts the subject, which is the prompted command's first line or else the dialog heading. `fm_composer_blocking_dialog` now reports these prompts as blocking dialogs, so the delivery guards no longer press Enter into them.\n- `bin/fm-watch.sh` adds `permission_prompt_check`. When the same prompt stays on an ordinary task's pane for `FM_PERMISSION_PROMPT_SECS` (default 90), it raises one `check: permission prompt pending` wake; secondmate panes are skipped. `fm_wake_queue_prune_task` now also prunes a task's `permission-prompt-<task>-<epoch>` wakes. Nothing answers the prompt.\n- The new `bin/fm-main-prompt-alarm.sh` runs from a `PermissionRequest` hook in `.claude/settings.json`. It alerts once when firstmate's own Claude main session waits on a permission prompt past `FM_MAIN_PROMPT_ALARM_SECS` (default 300). The wedge-alarm channel code moves out of `bin/fm-supervise-daemon.sh` into the new shared `bin/fm-wedge-alarm-lib.sh`, which both alarms use. Unit tests and an opt-in live e2e test (`tests/fm-permission-prompt-live-e2e.test.sh`) are added, and the docs and skills are updated to match.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n✅ Low: The change matches the stated intent and both earlier review fixes (secondmate panes get no prompt check; the moved comments now name bin/fm-supervise-daemon.sh). The new matcher only fires when the pane's last row is the \"Esc to cancel\" footer. The watcher check fires once per prompt, and the teardown prune matches only an all-digit suffix after the task id. The main-session hook prints nothing, so it never answers a prompt, and it is scoped to the lock-owning primary. The wedge-alarm channel code moved without behaviour changes apart from the title, which is now a parameter.\n\n## Testing\n\nI ran the opt-in live e2e against the installed Claude Code 2.1.307. I also built a marked lab home with a private tmux socket and drove a real Claude worker onto a hook-ask permission prompt. Against that pane, the real fm-send typed nothing and the prompt stayed open. The real fm-watch raised one `check: permission prompt pending: task=prompted ... waiting=6s - Claude permission prompt: echo fm-live-ask-marker && echo second-line` wake. A follow-up run did not wake again. After Escape cancelled the prompt, the next run raised no wake and the prompt records were cleared. I tore the lab down afterwards. The targeted deterministic tests also passed: the three new watcher cases, all six main-prompt-alarm cases, the composer fixtures, the typed-submit refusal, and the wake-queue prune. The paused-secondmate exemption and the main-alarm no-alert cases ran only in those deterministic tests, so they are reported as untested live. The evidence is CLI transcripts and tmux pane captures. This change has no graphical UI.\n\n- Live validation: ✅ go - 6 of 8 scenarios driven live against the product\n\n| Scenario | Result | Live | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A real Claude hook-ask permission prompt is recognized as a blocking dialog named after the prompted command&#39;s first line | ✅ pass | live | live-e2e-claude-2.1.307.log: &#39;the live hook-ask permission prompt matches and names the prompted command&#39; |\n| A primary session waiting on a prompt fires the PermissionRequest hook, which alerts once through the wedge-alarm channel and leaves the prompt unanswered | ✅ pass | live | live-e2e-claude-2.1.307.log: &#39;the PermissionRequest registration alerts on a waiting prompt and leaves it unanswered&#39; |\n| Steering a worker on a permission prompt with fm-send saves the steer to the inbox but types nothing and presses no Enter | ✅ pass | live | S2-fm-send.err (doorbell skipped, record 001.msg, rc 0) and S2-worker-pane-after-fm-send.txt (prompt still open, no steer text) |\n| The real watcher raises one `check: permission prompt pending` wake that names the task, window, wait time and command once a worker stays on the prompt past the threshold, and does not answer it | ✅ pass | live | S3-fm-watch.out, S3-worker-pane-after-watch.txt |\n| Adversarial: the same prompt does not wake twice | ✅ pass | live | S3c-fm-watch-repeat.out (watcher timed out, rc 124, with no wake) |\n| Adversarial: once the prompt is cancelled with Escape, the watcher raises no prompt wake and clears its records | ✅ pass | live | S4-fm-watch.out (no wake, rc 124), S4-prompt-records.txt (empty), S4-worker-pane-after-escape.txt |\n| Adversarial: a paused secondmate&#39;s pane on a permission prompt is not checked | ⏸️ untested | no | The prior payload did not establish a live result. This case ran only in the deterministic test (watch-triage-permission-tests.log: test_paused_secondmate_permission_prompt_is_not_checked), which uses… |\n| Adversarial: the main-session alarm stays quiet when the transcript moved on, the approved command is still running, a newer prompt replaced the old one, or the session holds no lock / is Cursor / is… | ⏸️ untested | no | The prior payload did not establish a live result. These quiet cases ran only in the repo&#39;s deterministic test (fm-main-prompt-alarm.log, 6 ok). Each one would need its own live run in a credentialed… |\n\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence: Live e2e transcript (Claude Code 2.1.307)</summary>\n\nSource: [Live e2e transcript (Claude Code 2.1.307)](https://github.com/johntran-mudflap/firstmate/blob/601e5428b7df06f7324cb0214ee30a33cf2055ff/.no-mistakes/evidence/fm/fm-permission-prompt-upstream/live-e2e-claude-2.1.307.log)\n\n```text\nok - Claude Code 2.1.307 (Claude Code): the live hook-ask permission prompt matches and names the prompted command\nok - Claude Code 2.1.307 (Claude Code): the PermissionRequest registration alerts on a waiting prompt and leaves it unanswered\n```\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence: Real Claude worker pane on the permission prompt</summary>\n\nSource: [Real Claude worker pane on the permission prompt](https://github.com/johntran-mudflap/firstmate/blob/601e5428b7df06f7324cb0214ee30a33cf2055ff/.no-mistakes/evidence/fm/fm-permission-prompt-upstream/S1-worker-pane-on-prompt.txt)\n\n```text\n╭─── Claude Code v2.1.153 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                                           │ Tips for getting started                                                                                         │\n│               Welcome back!               │ Run /init to create a CLAUDE.md file with instructions for Claude                                                │\n│                                           │ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │\n│                  ▐▛███▜▌                  │ What's new                                                                                                       │\n│                 ▝▜█████▛▘                 │ Added `/claude-api api-version` to move Claude API code to API version `2026-10-21`                              │\n│                   ▘▘ ▝▝                   │ Added the `claude_code.safety_event` OpenTelemetry event for each tool call a permission rule, auto mode, a saf… │\n│                                           │ Fixed requests failing with a model-not-found error when `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_1M_CONTEXT` is set and the model … │\n│           Haiku 4.5 · [redacted]          │ /release-notes for more                                                                                          │\n│     /…/T/fm-lab.WNA672/projects/work      │                                                                                                                  │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n  ⎿  SessionStart:startup hook error                                              ⎿  Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: lavish-axi: command not\n                                                                                     found\n  ⎿  SessionStart:startup hook error                                              ⎿  Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: gh-axi: command not found\n  ⎿  SessionStart:startup hook error                                              ⎿  Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: chrome-devtools-axi: command\n                                                                                      not found\n\n❯ Use the Bash tool to run exactly this one command and nothing else: echo fm-live-ask-marker && echo second-line\n\n⏺ Bash(echo fm-live-ask-marker && echo second-line)\n  ⎿  Waiting…\n\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n Bash command\n\n   echo fm-live-ask-marker && echo second-line\n   Run the requested echo commands\n\n Hook PreToolUse:Bash requires confirmation for this command:\n lab asks [settings]\n settings.json to update hooks\n\n Do you want to proceed?\n ❯ 1. Yes\n   2. No\n\n Esc to cancel · Tab to amend · ctrl+e to explain\n```\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence: fm-send output (doorbell skipped, steer saved to the inbox)</summary>\n\nSource: [fm-send output (doorbell skipped, steer saved to the inbox)](https://github.com/johntran-mudflap/firstmate/blob/601e5428b7df06f7324cb0214ee30a33cf2055ff/.no-mistakes/evidence/fm/fm-permission-prompt-upstream/S2-fm-send.err)\n\n```text\nfm-gate-refuse: gate agent lifecycle permitted only against lab home /private/var/folders/51/1351mbqd7jn0fjnv9l24y04c0000gn/T/fm-lab.WNA672\n●━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n●  WATCHER DOWN - SUPERVISION IS OFF\n●  1 task(s) in flight, but no watcher has a fresh beacon (last beat: never, grace 300s).\n●  Trust the emitted supervision protocol for this harness; do not use shell & for watcher repair.\n●  This is a supervision warning only; the requested message WILL still be sent.\n●  watcher supervision needs Stop-owned automatic recovery; inspect the hook registration and startup status before ending the turn.\n●━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nfm-send: doorbell skipped (composer visibly holds pending text); the steer is durably recorded at /private/var/folders/51/1351mbqd7jn0fjnv9l24y04c0000gn/T/fm-lab.WNA672/state/prompted.inbox/001.msg and the watcher will re-ring\n```\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence: Worker pane after fm-send: prompt still open, nothing typed</summary>\n\nSource: [Worker pane after fm-send: prompt still open, nothing typed](https://github.com/johntran-mudflap/firstmate/blob/601e5428b7df06f7324cb0214ee30a33cf2055ff/.no-mistakes/evidence/fm/fm-permission-prompt-upstream/S2-worker-pane-after-fm-send.txt)\n\n```text\n╭─── Claude Code v2.1.153 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                                           │ Tips for getting started                                                                                         │\n│               Welcome back!               │ Run /init to create a CLAUDE.md file with instructions for Claude                                                │\n│                                           │ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │\n│                  ▐▛███▜▌                  │ What's new                                                                                                       │\n│                 ▝▜█████▛▘                 │ Added `/claude-api api-version` to move Claude API code to API version `2026-10-21`                              │\n│                   ▘▘ ▝▝                   │ Added the `claude_code.safety_event` OpenTelemetry event for each tool call a permission rule, auto mode, a saf… │\n│                                           │ Fixed requests failing with a model-not-found error when `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_1M_CONTEXT` is set and the model … │\n│           Haiku 4.5 · [redacted]          │ /release-notes for more                                                                                          │\n│     /…/T/fm-lab.WNA672/projects/work      │                                                                                                                  │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n  ⎿  SessionStart:startup hook error                                              ⎿  Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: lavish-axi: command not\n                                                                                     found\n  ⎿  SessionStart:startup hook error                                              ⎿  Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: gh-axi: command not found\n  ⎿  SessionStart:startup hook error                                              ⎿  Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: chrome-devtools-axi: command\n                                                                                      not found\n\n❯ Use the Bash tool to run exactly this one command and nothing else: echo fm-live-ask-marker && echo second-line\n\n⏺ Bash(echo fm-live-ask-marker && echo second-line)\n  ⎿  Waiting…\n\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n Bash command\n\n   echo fm-live-ask-marker && echo second-line\n   Run the requested echo commands\n\n Hook PreToolUse:Bash requires confirmation for this command:\n lab asks [settings]\n settings.json to update hooks\n\n Do you want to proceed?\n ❯ 1. Yes\n   2. No\n\n Esc to cancel · Tab to amend · ctrl+e to explain\n```\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence: Real fm-watch wake sequence ending in the permission-prompt wake</summary>\n\nSource: [Real fm-watch wake sequence ending in the permission-prompt wake](https://github.com/johntran-mudflap/firstmate/blob/601e5428b7df06f7324cb0214ee30a33cf2055ff/.no-mistakes/evidence/fm/fm-permission-prompt-upstream/S3-fm-watch.out)\n\n<code>--- watcher run 2&#10;stale: fmlab:fm-prompted (blocked-on-prompt: Claude permission prompt: echo fm-live-ask-marker &amp;&amp; echo second-line)&#10;--- watcher run 3&#10;check: permission prompt pending: task=prompted window=fmlab:fm-prompted waiting=6s - Claude permission prompt: echo fm-live-ask-marker &amp;&amp; echo second-line</code>\n\n```text\n--- watcher run 1 rc=0 at 16:49:34\nsignal: /private/var/folders/51/1351mbqd7jn0fjnv9l24y04c0000gn/T/fm-lab.WNA672/state/prompted.status\n--- watcher run 2 rc=0 at 16:49:40\nstale: fmlab:fm-prompted (blocked-on-prompt: Claude permission prompt: echo fm-live-ask-marker && echo second-line)\n--- watcher run 3 rc=0 at 16:49:44\ncheck: permission prompt pending: task=prompted window=fmlab:fm-prompted waiting=6s - Claude permission prompt: echo fm-live-ask-marker && echo second-line\n```\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence: No repeat wake for the same prompt</summary>\n\nSource: [No repeat wake for the same prompt](https://github.com/johntran-mudflap/firstmate/blob/601e5428b7df06f7324cb0214ee30a33cf2055ff/.no-mistakes/evidence/fm/fm-permission-prompt-upstream/S3c-fm-watch-repeat.out)\n\n```text\nrc=124 (124 = timed out with no wake)\n```\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence: Pane after Escape and the quiet watcher run</summary>\n\nSource: [Pane after Escape and the quiet watcher run](https://github.com/johntran-mudflap/firstmate/blob/601e5428b7df06f7324cb0214ee30a33cf2055ff/.no-mistakes/evidence/fm/fm-permission-prompt-upstream/S4-worker-pane-after-escape.txt)\n\n```text\n╭─── Claude Code v2.1.153 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                                           │ Tips for getting started                                                                                         │\n│               Welcome back!               │ Run /init to create a CLAUDE.md file with instructions for Claude                                                │\n│                                           │ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │\n│                  ▐▛███▜▌                  │ What's new                                                                                                       │\n│                 ▝▜█████▛▘                 │ Added `/claude-api api-version` to move Claude API code to API version `2026-10-21`                              │\n│                   ▘▘ ▝▝                   │ Added the `claude_code.safety_event` OpenTelemetry event for each tool call a permission rule, auto mode, a saf… │\n│                                           │ Fixed requests failing with a model-not-found error when `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_1M_CONTEXT` is set and the model … │\n│           Haiku 4.5 · [redacted]          │ /release-notes for more                                                                                          │\n│     /…/T/fm-lab.WNA672/projects/work      │                                                                                                                  │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n  ⎿  SessionStart:startup hook error                                              ⎿  Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: lavish-axi: command not\n                                                                                     found\n  ⎿  SessionStart:startup hook error                                              ⎿  Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: gh-axi: command not found\n  ⎿  SessionStart:startup hook error                                              ⎿  Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: chrome-devtools-axi: command\n                                                                                      not found\n\n❯ Use the Bash tool to run exactly this one command and nothing else: echo fm-live-ask-marker && echo second-line\n\n⏺ Bash(echo fm-live-ask-marker && echo second-line)\n  ⎿  Interrupted · What should Claude do instead?\n\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n❯ \n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  ⏵⏵ bypass permissions on (shift+tab to cycle) · ← for agents                                                 Update available! Run: brew upgrade claude-code\n```\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence: New watcher permission-prompt test cases</summary>\n\nSource: [New watcher permission-prompt test cases](https://github.com/johntran-mudflap/firstmate/blob/601e5428b7df06f7324cb0214ee30a33cf2055ff/.no-mistakes/evidence/fm/fm-permission-prompt-upstream/watch-triage-permission-tests.log)\n\n```text\nok - a busy worker on a permission prompt wakes once past the threshold, naming the task and the command\nok - the permission prompt clock restarts for a different prompt and clears when the prompt leaves the pane\nok - a paused secondmate's pane is not checked for a pending permission prompt\nrc=0\n```\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence: Main-prompt-alarm alert and no-alert cases</summary>\n\nSource: [Main-prompt-alarm alert and no-alert cases](https://github.com/johntran-mudflap/firstmate/blob/601e5428b7df06f7324cb0214ee30a33cf2055ff/.no-mistakes/evidence/fm/fm-permission-prompt-upstream/fm-main-prompt-alarm.log)\n\n```text\nok - a main-session prompt still on screen alerts once through the wedge-alarm channels, and the hook decides nothing\nok - a prompt whose session transcript moved on does not alert\nok - an approved command still running, with an unchanged transcript, does not alert when the pane shows no prompt\nok - with no readable main pane the transcript decides alone, and the alert says so\nok - a newer prompt replaces the older one's record, so only the newer prompt's check alerts\nok - a session without the lock, a Cursor payload, a linked worktree, and a second mate's home record and alert nothing\nfm-main-prompt-alarm rc=0\n```\n</details>\n\n## Pipeline\n\nUpdates from [git push no-mistakes](https://github.com/kunchenguid/no-mistakes)\n\n<!-- no-mistakes-pipeline-attestation:v1 {\"head_sha\":\"4c60946a388715d1cfb0a65865f4c2193b0ca0c1\",\"steps\":[{\"step\":\"intent\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"step\":\"rebase\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"step\":\"review\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"step\":\"test\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"step\":\"document\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"step\":\"lint\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"step\":\"push\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"step\":\"pr\",\"status\":\"running\"},{\"step\":\"ci\",\"status\":\"pending\"}],\"live_validation\":{\"verdict\":\"go\",\"live\":6,\"total\":8}} -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **intent** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Rebase** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Review** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Test** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n- Live validation: ✅ go - 6 of 8 scenarios driven live against the product\n\n| Scenario | Result | Live | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A real Claude hook-ask permission prompt is recognized as a blocking dialog named after the prompted command&#39;s first line | ✅ pass | live | live-e2e-claude-2.1.307.log: &#39;the live hook-ask permission prompt matches and names the prompted command&#39; |\n| A primary session waiting on a prompt fires the PermissionRequest hook, which alerts once through the wedge-alarm channel and leaves the prompt unanswered | ✅ pass | live | live-e2e-claude-2.1.307.log: &#39;the PermissionRequest registration alerts on a waiting prompt and leaves it unanswered&#39; |\n| Steering a worker on a permission prompt with fm-send saves the steer to the inbox but types nothing and presses no Enter | ✅ pass | live | S2-fm-send.err (doorbell skipped, record 001.msg, rc 0) and S2-worker-pane-after-fm-send.txt (prompt still open, no steer text) |\n| The real watcher raises one `check: permission prompt pending` wake that names the task, window, wait time and command once a worker stays on the prompt past the threshold, and does not answer it | ✅ pass | live | S3-fm-watch.out, S3-worker-pane-after-watch.txt |\n| Adversarial: the same prompt does not wake twice | ✅ pass | live | S3c-fm-watch-repeat.out (watcher timed out, rc 124, with no wake) |\n| Adversarial: once the prompt is cancelled with Escape, the watcher raises no prompt wake and clears its records | ✅ pass | live | S4-fm-watch.out (no wake, rc 124), S4-prompt-records.txt (empty), S4-worker-pane-after-escape.txt |\n| Adversarial: a paused secondmate&#39;s pane on a permission prompt is not checked | ⏸️ untested | no | The prior payload did not establish a live result. This case ran only in the deterministic test (watch-triage-permission-tests.log: test_paused_secondmate_permission_prompt_is_not_checked), which uses… |\n| Adversarial: the main-session alarm stays quiet when the transcript moved on, the approved command is still running, a newer prompt replaced the old one, or the session holds no lock / is Cursor / is… | ⏸️ untested | no | The prior payload did not establish a live result. These quiet cases ran only in the repo&#39;s deterministic test (fm-main-prompt-alarm.log, 6 ok). Each one would need its own live run in a credentialed… |\n\n- <code>`FM_PERMISSION_PROMPT_LIVE_E2E=1 bash tests/fm-permission-prompt-live-e2e.test.sh` (real Claude Code 2.1.307 TUI, isolated tmux socket)</code>\n- <code>Live lab script: `bin/fm-lab-home.sh create $LAB`, real `claude --model haiku` worker pane on the `fm-lab` socket on a PreToolUse-ask prompt, then real `bin/fm-send.sh prompted &#34;please continue...&#34;` with FM_HOME=$LAB</code>\n- <code>Live lab: real `bin/fm-watch.sh` (FM_PERMISSION_PROMPT_SECS=6) run repeatedly with `bin/fm-wake-drain.sh` acks until the prompt wake; one more run to confirm no repeat wake</code>\n- <code>Live lab: sent Escape to the worker pane, re-ran `bin/fm-watch.sh` (FM_PERMISSION_PROMPT_SECS=1) and checked that no wake fired and the prompt records were cleared</code>\n- <code>The 3 new permission-prompt cases from `tests/fm-watch-triage.test.sh` (busy-pane wake once, clock restart and clear, paused secondmate not checked), run from a temporary filtered copy that was then removed</code>\n- `bash tests/fm-main-prompt-alarm.test.sh`\n- `bash tests/fm-composer-lib.test.sh`\n- `bash tests/fm-tmux-submit-busy.test.sh`\n- `bash tests/fm-wake-queue.test.sh`\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Document** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚠️ **Lint** - 1 warning</summary>\n\n- ⚠️ linter found issues (exit code 1)\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Push** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"act